-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Boundary Discontinuities:** Naive partitioning leads to visible seams. The method requires explicit alignment of adjacent NeRFs [S3].
-*   **Scalability:** The method decouples rendering time from scene size, allowing it to scale to arbitrarily large environments [S3].
+**Edge Cases:**
+-   **Boundary Discontinuities:** Rendering at block boundaries requires careful handling of transmittance continuity to avoid visual artifacts [S3].
+-   **Degenerate Input:** If a block has no training data (e.g., occluded or out of view), the MLP may not converge properly.
 
